{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And HaShem will remove from you every illness</b> — that commonly comes upon the world. And He mentioned every malady of Egypt, the evil ones, to promise, and He will place them upon all who hate you. Or perhaps it alludes that when they fulfill the statutes they will be saved from them, and if they do not fulfill them, these will come upon them just as they came upon the Egyptians, as stated in the admonitions (Deuteronomy 28:60): \"and He will bring back upon you all the maladies of Egypt,\" etc., and I have already explained this in the portion of Beshalach (Exodus 15:26). And He mentioned first, among the statutes, to destroy and to exterminate the worshippers of idols, and therefore He said, \"and you shall eat all the peoples\" — that you shall exterminate them, in the sense of what is said, \"for they are our bread\" (Numbers 14:9), \"for he has eaten up Jacob\" (Psalms 79:7), \"they have devoured him and consumed him\" (Jeremiah 10:25), and so many others. And He said, \"your eye shall have no pity on them,\" as I have already mentioned (Ramban on Deuteronomy 7:12), for through the compassion of the judges the entire statute is lost."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The reading השופטים ('the judges') appears in standard editions; the variant הטפשים ('the fools') is noted in some witnesses. I have translated according to the primary reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:40.181749918Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}